From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 07:52:53 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] contrib: provide tested structured logging collector
 configurations

Add Alloy file and native-journal, Promtail, Vector, Fluent Bit and rsyslog examples. Keep identifiers and addresses in record bodies; label only severity, category and a static job. Document durable reader state and the daemon format mapping.

Ran actual isolated Linux arm64 tools: Alloy 1.8.3 and Promtail 3.4.2 into Loki 3.4.2, Vector 0.45.0 and Fluent Bit 4.0.0 into JSON console, rsyslog 8.2504.0 into parsed JSONL. All 53 records retained recursive field values/types across six pipelines, including three native journal multiline/NUL records. These are collector/component checks, not a full Linux daemon run. Google Cloud Logging was checked against its schema only; no cloud ingestion test.

(cherry picked from commit acc94e134b98231ac526f001911969d791253bbc)

